<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <!-- SEO Meta Tags -->
    {#- Two strings, one source. `pageHeading` is what the page is called
        ("Mob of the Dead Easter Egg Guide"); `pageTitle` is that plus the game,
        which exists to disambiguate one search result from another. The suffix
        belongs in <title> and nowhere else: in the <h1> it dilutes the heading
        Google reads as a content signal, and it eats room in the sticky top bar
        between the Home and legend buttons on a phone. Deriving one from the
        other keeps them from drifting apart the way two literals would. #}
    {%- if mapName and solverTitle %}
        {%- set pageHeading = mapName + ' ' + solverTitle %}
    {%- elif mapName %}
        {%- set pageHeading = mapName + ' Easter Egg Guide' %}
    {%- else %}
        {%- set pageHeading = title %}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- set pageTitle = (pageHeading + ' | ' + titleSuffix) if mapName else pageHeading %}
    <title>{{ pageTitle }}</title>

    {#- These fallbacks fire for any page with no `description` of its own, and
        they used to run 177-183 chars once a real map name and game were
        substituted in, which is past the ~155 Google will show. The three
        Tortured Path survival maps shipped truncated for exactly that reason.
        Kept short enough that even the longest name and game on the site
        ("Attack of the Radioactive Thing", "Black Ops Cold War Zombies") lands
        inside the budget, so a new page can never inherit a clipped one. -#}
    {%- if mapName and solverTitle %}
        {%- set metaDescription = description or 'Interactive ' + solverTitle + ' for ' + mapName + ' in ' + titleSuffix + '. Solve this main quest step in seconds.' %}
    {%- elif mapName %}
        {%- set metaDescription = description or 'Complete ' + mapName + ' Easter Egg guide for ' + titleSuffix + '. Step-by-step main quest walkthrough with pictures and video.' %}
    {%- else %}
        {%- set metaDescription = description or 'Complete Call of Duty Zombies Easter Egg guide. Step-by-step main quest walkthrough with pictures, videos, and detailed instructions.' %}
    {%- endif %}
    {#- `aliases` used to be appended here as " Also known as X, Y." Two reasons
        it is gone: it landed at the very end of the string, which is the first
        thing Google truncates, so on the long descriptions it never reached the
        snippet at all; and a meta description is not a ranking input, so the
        terms earned nothing there. Aliases now go two better places instead:
        woven into the hand-written `description` early enough to survive the
        cut, and rendered in full into the About This Map copy below, which is
        indexable body text. -#}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
    {%- if mapName %}
        {%- set metaKeywords = mapName + ' Easter Egg, ' + mapName + ' Easter Egg guide, ' + mapName + ' main quest, ' + mapName + ' main Easter Egg, ' + mapName + ' walkthrough, ' + mapName + ' guide, ' + mapName + ' steps, ' + mapName + ' tutorial, ' + mapName + ' solo Easter Egg, ' + titleSuffix + ', Call of Duty Zombies, COD Zombies, Zombies Easter Egg guide, main quest walkthrough' %}
        <meta name="keywords" content="{{ metaKeywords }}">
    {%- endif %}
    <meta name="author" content="mmmrkennedy">
    {#- Which deploy produced this page. Read by ts/ui/line-flagger.ts and stored
        on solver flags, so a report can be told apart from one filed against
        code that has since been fixed. -#}
    <meta name="build" content="{{ site.buildVersion }}">
    {#- One switch decides whether a map is live: `class="disabled"` on its link
        in src/index.html, which _data/unfinishedPages.js reads. That is already
        what stops the sitemap listing a page, what keeps it out of the related-
        maps blocks, and what hides the "Full X Map Guide" link on a solver page,
        so it decides the noindex and the placeholder body below too. Launching a
        guide is removing that one class.

        This used to read `unfinished or page.url in unfinishedPages`, and the
        second half could never be true: page.url carries the .html the index
        hrefs leave off, so no page path ever equalled a registry entry (and
        before the fix in unfinishedPages.js the entries were "//games/..."
        besides). Every stub was held up by the `unfinished: true` in its own
        front matter alone, which meant two lists that had to agree and no
        warning if they ever stopped. `| cleanUrl` normalises both sides the same
        way the canonical URL below does, and the front-matter flag is gone from
        all 17 guides that carried it. -#}
    {%- if page.url | cleanUrl in unfinishedPages %}
        <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    {%- else %}
        <meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1">
    {%- endif %}
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}">

    <!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="article">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ ogImage or 'https://mmmrkennedy.com/og_image.png' }}">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="mmmrkennedy's Zombies Guides">

    <!-- Twitter Card -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:url" content="https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ ogImage or 'https://mmmrkennedy.com/og_image.png' }}">

    <!-- Stylesheets -->
    {%- if site.bundled %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/bundle.min.css?v={{ site.buildVersion }}">
    {%- else %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/styles.css?v={{ site.buildVersion }}">
    {%- endif %}
    {#- Only the stats page uses these rules, so they are not in the bundle —
        see the note in css/styles.css. #}
    {%- if statsPage %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/stats.css?v={{ site.buildVersion }}">
    {%- endif %}
    {#- On a solver-only page the solver IS the content, so its stylesheet blocks
        first paint like any other. In a guide the solver sits thousands of words
        below the fold, and blocking paint on 20KB that styles nothing visible
        costs ~70ms of FCP on a throttled phone. There it loads async instead:
        media="print" makes the browser fetch the sheet at low priority while it
        matches no screen, and onload flips it to all the moment it lands.
        No <noscript> fallback — the solver is React, so with JS off there is
        nothing on the page for these rules to style. #}
    {%- if useSolverCSS %}
        {%- if solverIsPrimary %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/Solvers.css?v={{ site.buildVersion }}">
        {%- else %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/Solvers.css?v={{ site.buildVersion }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all';this.onload=null">
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}

    <!-- AdSense: site-verification meta only. The adsbygoogle.js loader is
         injected by src/ts/ui/ads.ts the moment a real slot is pushed, so a page
         that renders no ads never contacts Google. -->
    <meta name="google-adsense-account" content="ca-pub-2164582284838563">

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon/favicon.ico">
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//www.youtube.com">
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//discord.com">
    {%- if preloadImages %}
        {%- for imgSrc in preloadImages %}
        <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ imgSrc }}">
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- endif %}
    {#- Preload only where the solver is the reason for the visit. Unconditional,
        this preloaded a 78KB Preact bundle at high priority on all 80 pages while
        only 18 ever ran it; narrowed to those 18, it still put the bundle — the
        largest asset on a guide — into the same millisecond as the CSS that
        blocks first paint, for a widget nobody has scrolled to yet. Worth ~50ms
        of FCP on a throttled phone. The <script> near the end of <body> is not
        conditioned on this and still loads it there, just without jumping the
        queue ahead of the page the reader actually came for. #}
    {%- if useReactSolvers and solverIsPrimary %}
    <!-- REACT_BUNDLE_MODULEPRELOAD -->
    {%- endif %}

    <!-- JSON-LD Structured Data -->
    {#- Article, not HowTo. This was HowTo until 2026-08-15, which earned nothing:
        Google retired HowTo rich results entirely, and the block never carried the
        `step` array HowTo requires anyway, so it validated as a bare entity with no
        eligible treatment. Article is the type these pages actually are, and it is
        the one Google still reads dates and author from. The BreadcrumbList below
        is untouched — that one does still produce a rich result.

        datePublished/dateModified come from the same filters the footer prints, so
        the date in the SERP and the date on the page can never disagree. #}
    {%- set articlePublished = page.inputPath | releasedISO %}
    {%- set articleModified = page.inputPath | lastmodISO %}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
        {
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "Article",
            {#- Heading, not title: the game name is already in `publisher` and
                `about`, so the suffix would just repeat it a third time. #}
            "name": "{{ pageHeading }}",
            "headline": "{{ pageHeading }}",
            {%- if mapName %}
            {#- On a solver page the alias belongs to the solver, not the guide:
                "COTD Easter Egg Guide" names a different page from the one this
                schema describes. `solverTitle` is exactly the words that follow
                the map name in the heading, so it yields the alternate name a
                reader would actually type. -#}
            {%- set altSuffix = solverTitle if solverTitle else 'Easter Egg Guide' %}
            "alternateName": [{% for alias in aliases %}"{{ alias }} {{ altSuffix }}", {% endfor %}"{{ mapName }} {{ altSuffix }}"],
            "keywords": "{{ metaKeywords }}",
            {%- endif %}
            "description": "{{ metaDescription }}",
            "url": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}",
            "mainEntityOfPage": {
                "@type": "WebPage",
                "@id": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}"
            },
            "image": "{{ ogImage or 'https://mmmrkennedy.com/og_image.png' }}",
            {%- if articlePublished %}
            "datePublished": "{{ articlePublished }}",
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if articleModified %}
            "dateModified": "{{ articleModified }}",
            {%- endif %}
            "author": {
                "@type": "Person",
                "name": "mmmrkennedy",
                "url": "https://mmmrkennedy.com"
            },
            "publisher": {
                "@type": "Organization",
                "name": "mmmrkennedy's Zombies Guides",
                "url": "https://mmmrkennedy.com"
            },
            "genre": "Gaming Guide",
            "about": {
                "@type": "VideoGame",
                "name": "Call of Duty Zombies"
            }
        }
    </script>

    {%- if breadcrumb %}
        <script type="application/ld+json">
            {
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
                "itemListElement": [
                    {
                        "@type": "ListItem",
                        "position": 1,
                        "name": "Home",
                        "item": "https://mmmrkennedy.com/"
                    }
            {%- for crumb in breadcrumb -%}
        ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ loop.index + 1 }},
            "name": "{{ crumb.name }}",
            "item": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ crumb.url }}"
        }
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if solverTitle %}
        ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ breadcrumb | length + 2 }},
            "name": "{{ mapName }}",
            "item": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ guideUrl | cleanUrl }}"
        }
        ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ breadcrumb | length + 3 }},
            "name": "{{ solverTitle }}",
            "item": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}"
        }
        {%- else %}
        ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ breadcrumb | length + 2 }},
            "name": "{{ mapName or pageTitle }}",
            "item": "https://mmmrkennedy.com{{ page.url | cleanUrl }}"
        }
        {%- endif %}
            ]
        }
        </script>
    {%- endif %}
</head>

<body{% if skipTOC %} data-skip-toc="true"{% endif %}{% if noFlags %} data-no-flags{% endif %}{% if statsPage %} data-stats-live{% endif %}>
<div class="top-buttons-background-box">
    <!-- Title at the top of the page -->
    <h1 class="title-text">{{ pageHeading }}</h1>
    {%- if not noLegend %}
    <button type="button" id="legendLauncher" class="btn legend-launcher"
            aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="legendOverlay"
            aria-label="How to read this guide">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
            <path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3" />
            <path d="M12 17h.01" />
        </svg>
    </button>
    {%- endif %}

    <!-- Mobile devices content -->
    <div id="mobile-content">
        {#- An anchor, not a button. `navigateToIndex()` only ever set
            location.href = "/", so the behaviour is identical, but a <button
            onclick> is invisible to a crawler: it left every guide page with no
            followable link back to the index, and the site with a link graph
            that ran one way and stopped. #}
        <a class="btn btn--link btn--fixed top-left" href="/">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-arrow-left-icon lucide-circle-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
                <path d="m12 8-4 4 4 4" />
                <path d="M16 12H8" />
            </svg>
            <span class="visually-hidden">Home</span>
        </a>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--fixed bottom-right" onclick="window.ScrollManager.scrollToTop()" aria-label="Back to Top">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-to-line-icon lucide-arrow-up-to-line" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M5 3h14" />
                <path d="m18 13-6-6-6 6" />
                <path d="M12 7v14" />
            </svg>
        </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Non-mobile devices content -->
    <div id="non-mobile-content">
        <a class="btn btn--link btn--fixed top-left" href="/">Home</a>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--fixed bottom-right" onclick="window.ScrollManager.scrollToTop()">Back to Top</button>
    </div>

    <div class="version-display">
        <div class="version-and-toggle">
            <button type="button" id="ad-toggle-btn" class="ad-toggle-btn" aria-pressed="true">Hide Ads</button>
            <span id="ad-mode-indicator" class="ad-mode-indicator"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="content-window{% if not statsPage %} prose{% endif %}">
    {#- The guide body, and nothing that repeats from page to page. The footer
        stays outside: a <footer> inside <main> loses its contentinfo landmark
        role, so nesting it would trade one landmark for another. #}
    <main>
    {%- if page.url | cleanUrl in unfinishedPages %}
        <div class="content-container">
            <h2>Sorry, this page is not ready yet!</h2>
            <p>Please check back later.</p>
        </div>
    {%- else %}
        {{ content | safe }}
        {%- if about %}
        <section class="about-map">
            <h2 class="about-map__title">About This Map</h2>
            {#- The community shorthand for a map is often the only name people
                search by, and until now `aliases` reached the meta description
                and JSON-LD alternateName and nothing else. Neither is a ranking
                input, so "MOTD" appeared nowhere Google could weigh it: not once
                on the whole Mob of the Dead page. Rendering the same front
                matter here puts it in indexable body copy, and keeps the visible
                names and the meta names from drifting apart. -#}
            <p class="about-map__text">{{ about }}{% if aliases %} Also known as {{ aliases | join(', ') }}.{% endif %}</p>
        </section>
        {%- endif %}
        {#- Sibling maps from the same game, from src/_data/relatedMaps.js. The
            one link every guide had to another page was /stats in the footer,
            which meant no guide passed any authority to another and nothing
            grouped a map with the rest of its game. Unfinished maps are absent
            by construction: they are noindex stubs, so linking them would only
            spend crawl budget on a placeholder. #}
        {%- set related = relatedMaps[page.url | cleanUrl] %}
        {%- if related %}
        <nav class="related-maps" aria-labelledby="related-maps-title">
            <h2 class="related-maps__title" id="related-maps-title">More Zombies guides</h2>
            <div class="related-maps__groups">
                {%- for group in related.groups %}
                <div class="related-maps__group">
                    <p class="related-maps__group-label">{{ group.gameName }}</p>
                    <ul class="related-maps__list">
                        {%- for map in group.maps %}
                        <li><a class="related-maps__link" href="{{ map.url }}">{{ map.title }}</a></li>
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </div>
                {%- endfor %}
            </div>
            <p class="related-maps__all"><a class="related-maps__link" href="/">All Call of Duty Zombies map guides</a></p>
        </nav>
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
        {%- set updated = page.inputPath | lastmod %}
        {%- set updatedISO = page.inputPath | lastmodISO %}
        {%- set updatedRel = page.inputPath | lastmodRelative %}
        {%- set released = page.inputPath | released %}
        {%- set releasedISO = page.inputPath | releasedISO %}
        {%- set releasedRel = page.inputPath | releasedRelative %}
        {%- set edits = page.inputPath | editcount %}
        {%- set editorList = editors | formatEditors %}
        {#- A page the index still marks disabled shows the placeholder above
            instead of `content`, so it must not advertise the word count of a
            body nobody can read. #}
        {%- set words = null if (noWordCount or page.url | cleanUrl in unfinishedPages) else (content | wordcount) %}
        <p class="site-footer__meta">
            <span class="site-footer__copyright">&copy; {% year %} mmmrkennedy</span>
            {%- if editorList %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="site-footer__editors">Edited by {{ editorList }}</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if released %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><time class="site-footer__released" datetime="{{ releasedISO }}" title="Released {{ releasedRel }}">Initial release {{ released }}</time>{% endif %}
            {%- if updated %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><time class="site-footer__updated" datetime="{{ updatedISO }}" title="Last updated {{ updated }}">Updated {{ updatedRel }}</time>{% endif %}
            {%- if edits %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="site-footer__edits">{{ edits }} edit{{ "s" if edits != 1 }}</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if words %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="site-footer__words">{{ words | thousands }} words</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if not statsPage %}<span class="site-footer__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span><a class="site-footer__link" href="/stats">Site stats</a>{% endif %}
            <span class="site-footer__views"></span>
        </p>
        {#- CC BY-SA 3.0 asks for credit "in any reasonable manner based on the
            medium", which for a web page means somewhere a reader can actually
            find it. Shown only where the artwork is: the queen glyph is a
            background-image in Solvers.css, so it can only appear on a page
            that loads it. See the licence note at .queens-cell.is-queen. #}
        {%- if useSolverCSS %}
        <p class="site-footer__credits">
            Chess queen icon by <a class="site-footer__link" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Cburnett" rel="noopener">Cburnett</a>, used unmodified under <a class="site-footer__link" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" rel="license noopener">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>.
        </p>
        {%- endif %}
    </footer>
</div>


